  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Find those integral values of m for which the x-coordinate (printed ''c-coordinate'') of the point of intersection of the lines y = mx + 1 and 3x + 4y = 9 is an integer. (3 marks)', 'Substituting y = mx + 1 in 3x + 4y = 9: 3x + 4mx + 4 = 9, so x(3 + 4m) = 5 and x = 5/(3 + 4m). For x to be an integer, 3 + 4m must be a divisor of 5: ±1 or ±5. 3 + 4m = 1 → m = −1/2; 3 + 4m = −1 → m = −1; 3 + 4m = 5 → m = 1/2; 3 + 4m = −5 → m = −2. The integral values are m = −1 (x = −5) and m = −2 (x = −1).', null, '[{"point": "Substitute: 3x + 4(mx + 1) = 9 → x(3 + 4m) = 5 → x = 5/(3 + 4m)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "x is an integer when 3 + 4m ∈ {±1, ±5}", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Integral m: 3 + 4m = −1 → m = −1; 3 + 4m = −5 → m = −2 (others give m = ±1/2) → m = −1, −2", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
