  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Define the term solution. How many types of solutions are formed? Write briefly about each type with an example. (3 marks)', 'A solution is a homogeneous mixture of two or more components whose composition is uniform throughout; the component in larger amount is the solvent, the other the solute.
Based on the physical state of the solvent there are three types (nine in all by solute/ solvent state):
1. Gaseous solutions (solvent a gas): gas in gas - air (O₂ and N₂); liquid in gas - chloroform vapour in N₂; solid in gas - camphor in N₂.
2. Liquid solutions (solvent a liquid): gas in liquid - O₂ dissolved in water, soda water (CO₂); liquid in liquid - ethanol in water; solid in liquid - sugar or salt in water.
3. Solid solutions (solvent a solid): gas in solid - H₂ in palladium; liquid in solid - mercury in sodium (amalgam); solid in solid - alloys such as brass (Zn in Cu).', null, '[{"point": "Solution: homogeneous mixture of two or more substances (solute + solvent)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Nine types by the states of solute and solvent (gas, liquid, solid in gaseous, liquid and solid solvents) - or three broad types: gaseous, liquid, solid solutions", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Examples: gaseous - air; liquid - sugar or salt in water, ethanol in water, O₂ in water; solid - alloys (brass), H₂ in palladium, amalgam", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
