  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'The circuit arrangement in the figure shows that when an alternating current passes through coil A, a current starts flowing in coil B. (i) State the underlying principle involved. (ii) Mention two factors on which the current produced in coil B depends. (3 marks)', '(i) The principle is mutual induction (Faraday''s law of electromagnetic induction). The alternating current in coil A produces a continuously changing magnetic field; the changing flux linked with coil B induces an emf in B, which drives a current through its circuit (shown by the galvanometer).
(ii) The current in coil B depends on: the number of turns in the coils; the rate of change of current in coil A (its frequency and amplitude); the separation and relative orientation of the two coils (how much flux links them); a soft-iron core between them, which increases the mutual inductance; and the resistance of coil B''s circuit.', null, '[{"point": "(i) Mutual induction (electromagnetic induction, Faraday''s law): the changing current in A produces a changing magnetic flux linked with B, inducing an emf in B", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "(ii) Any two: number of turns of the coils, rate of change of current in A (frequency/ amplitude), distance and orientation between the coils (coupling), presence of a soft-iron core, resistance of coil B''s circuit", "marks": 1.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
