  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Read each statement below carefully and state, with reasons, if it is true or false. A particle in one-dimensional motion (a) with zero speed at an instant may have non-zero acceleration at that instant; (b) with constant speed must have zero acceleration. (3 marks)', '(a) True. At the highest point of a ball thrown vertically upwards its speed is momentarily zero, but its acceleration is still g (9.8 m/s² downwards).
